# GramSetu Root Environment Configuration Overview
# GramSetu consists of three decoupled components, each with its own .env.example:
#
# 1. API Server (server/.env):
#    - Copy server/.env.example to server/.env
#    - Requires: MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET (min 32 chars), CLIENT_ORIGINS
#    - Optional: GEMINI_API_KEY, CLOUDINARY_*, SEGMENTATION_SERVICE_URL, SEED_DB
#
# 2. Web Client (client/.env):
#    - Copy client/.env.example to client/.env
#    - Optional: VITE_API_BASE_URL (defaults to direct proxy /api)
#
# 3. Defect Detection Service (segmentation-service/.env):
#    - Copy segmentation-service/.env.example to segmentation-service/.env
#    - Optional: SEGMENTATION_ENV=development, MODEL_PATH=models/model.onnx
#
# For local development with demo data:
# 1. In server/.env set:
#    JWT_SECRET=your_local_development_jwt_secret_at_least_32_characters_long
#    MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/gramsetu (or local replica set / Atlas)
#    SEED_DB=true
# 2. Run: npm run install:all
# 3. Run: npm run dev
